 "stem": "$ABCD$ is a parallelogram where $A({=ax}, {=ay})$, $B({=bx}, {=by})$ and $C({=cx}, {=cy})$. Find the coordinates of the vertex $D$.",
 "solution": [
  "The diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other, so the midpoint of $\\overline{AC}$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{BD}$.",
  "Midpoint of $\\overline{AC}$ = $\\left(\\frac{{={ax}}+{={cx}}}{2}, \\frac{{={ay}}+{={cy}}}{2}\\right)$.",
  "Let $D(x, y)$. Then $\\frac{{={bx}}+x}{2} = \\frac{{={ax+cx}}}{2}$, so $x = {=dx}$.",
  "Also $\\frac{{={by}}+y}{2} = \\frac{{={ay+cy}}}{2}$, so $y = {=dy}$.",
  "So $D({=dx}, {=dy})$."
 ],
